    <encodingDesc>
      <projectDesc>
        <p>This regularized edition normalizes 18th-century French prerevolutionary orthography and expands abbreviations using parallel TEI choice markup (method="markup"). Historical diplomatic readings are preserved in orig, sic, and abbr, while regularized forms are supplied in reg, corr, and expan with editorial attribution (@resp="#editor" and @resp="#gemini"). Imperfect verb forms ending in -ois and -oit are regularized to -ais and -ait per the 1835 Académie française reform, while invariant nouns ending in -oit (such as droit) are strictly preserved. Missing accents on capitalized words and historical prepositions are restored. Named entities link to authority records via compact @ref CURIEs: wikidata: (https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/) and geonames: (https://www.geonames.org/).</p>
      </projectDesc>
    </encodingDesc>
